192 0 obj
<<
/Type /StructElem
/S /H2
/P 75 0 R
/T (During my internship at Schneider Electric's Switchgear Design and Development Center, I worked on a project to create a Door Interlock System for the draw-out EOM Module door. This system aimed to enhance safety by preventing the door from opening until the isolated position was reached, while also allowing for a temporary defeat feature for testing purposes. When the door was opened in this state, it would self-lock upon closure. Additionally, the system enabled a smooth draw-out of the EOM Module and prevented users from resetting any features after reinsertion. )
/E (During my internship at Schneider Electric's Switchgear Design and Development Center, I worked on a project to create a Door Interlock System for the draw-out EOM Module door. This system aimed to enhance safety by preventing the door from opening until the isolated position was reached, while also allowing for a temporary defeat feature for testing purposes. When the door was opened in this state, it would self-lock upon closure. Additionally, the system enabled a smooth draw-out of the EOM Module and prevented users from resetting any features after reinsertion. )
/Pg 21 0 R
/K [5]
>>
endobj
193 0 obj
<<
/Type /StructElem
/S /H2
/P 75 0 R
/T (The project's scope was extensive, addressing multiple requirements, with safety and precision as top priorities. The Door Interlock System had to withstand substantial stress levels, serving as a robust door lock against users. This project showcased Schneider Electric's commitment to innovative solutions, emphasizing safety and precision.)
/E (The project's scope was extensive, addressing multiple requirements, with safety and precision as top priorities. The Door Interlock System had to withstand substantial stress levels, serving as a robust door lock against users. This project showcased Schneider Electric's commitment to innovative solutions, emphasizing safety and precision.)
/Pg 21 0 R
/K [6]
>>
endobj
